STORIES_LOAD("gn",{"gn1":{"icon":"🌍","passage":[[1,1,31],[2,1,3]],"intro":[{"sc":"cosmos","n":"Before anything existed, there was only God. No sun, no earth, no people. Just darkness, and God."},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"Then God spoke. \"Let there be light!\" And there was light."},{"sc":"earthday","n":"Over six days, God made the sky, the seas, dry land, plants, the sun, moon and stars, fish, birds and animals. And He said it was good."},{"sc":"earthday","n":"Last of all, God made people, in His own image. And He said it was VERY good. On the seventh day, God rested."}],"lesson":{"title":"You were made on purpose","text":"Everything you see was made by God, and you were made in His image. That means you're not an accident. You have value, and you were made to reflect God's goodness."},"order":["God makes light","God makes the sky and the seas","God makes plants and trees","God makes the sun, moon and stars","God makes fish and birds","God makes animals and people","God rests"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did God make on the first day?","o":["Light","Animals","People","The sun"],"why":"\"Let there be light\" came first."},{"q":"In whose image were people made?","o":["God's image","The angels' image","The animals' image","Nobody's"],"why":"Genesis 1:27: \"in the image of God he made him\"."},{"q":"What did God do on the seventh day?","o":["He rested","He made the sea","He made people","He made the stars"],"why":"God rested, and blessed the seventh day."}],"words":["LIGHT","SEA","STARS","PLANTS","REST","GOOD"]},"gn2":{"icon":"🍎","passage":[[2,7,9],[2,15,25],[3,1,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"garden","n":"God made a beautiful garden called Eden, full of trees and rivers. He put Adam there to look after it."},{"sc":"garden","n":"Adam could eat from every tree except one: the tree of the knowledge of good and evil. God made Eve to be his partner."},{"sc":"garden","n":"Then a crafty snake came to Eve with a question: \"Did God really say...?\""},{"sc":"garden","n":"Eve and Adam ate the forbidden fruit. Suddenly they felt ashamed, and hid from God. Sin had entered the world."}],"lesson":{"title":"Listen to God's voice first","text":"The snake didn't start with a lie. It started with a question that made God's words sound unclear. Adam and Eve listened to the wrong voice. But even after they failed, God came looking for them and promised a rescue."},"order":["God puts Adam in the garden","God makes Eve","The snake asks Eve a tricky question","Eve and Adam eat the forbidden fruit","They hide from God","God sends them out of the garden"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which tree were Adam and Eve told not to eat from?","o":["The tree of the knowledge of good and evil","The apple tree","The tree of life","The palm tree"],"why":"Genesis 2:17."},{"q":"Who said, \"Where are you?\"","o":["The Lord God","The snake","Adam","Eve"],"why":"Genesis 3:9. God came looking for them."},{"q":"How did the snake begin tempting Eve?","o":["With a question about what God really said","With a gift","With a threat","With a song"],"why":"\"Has God truly said...?\""}],"words":["EDEN","SNAKE","FRUIT","TREE","ADAM","EVE"]},"gn3":{"icon":"🐑","passage":[[4,1,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"field2","n":"Adam and Eve had two sons. Cain grew crops. Abel looked after sheep."},{"sc":"field2","n":"Both brought gifts to God. Abel brought the very best of his flock. God was pleased with Abel's gift, but not with Cain's."},{"sc":"field2","n":"Cain became very angry and jealous. God warned him: sin is waiting at the door, but you must rule over it."},{"sc":"field2","n":"Cain didn't listen. He attacked his brother, and Abel died. God asked Cain where his brother was."}],"lesson":{"title":"Rule over anger before it rules you","text":"God warned Cain before he did anything wrong. Anger and jealousy were like an animal waiting at the door. Cain could have stopped it. Leaders learn to notice anger early, talk to God about it, and choose not to let it win."},"order":["Cain grows crops and Abel keeps sheep","Both bring gifts to God","God is pleased with Abel's gift","Cain becomes angry and jealous","God warns Cain about sin at the door","God asks Cain, \"Where is your brother?\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Abel give to God?","o":["The best of his flock","Some fruit","Gold","Nothing"],"why":"He gave God his best."},{"q":"What did God say was waiting at the door?","o":["Sin","A lion","A friend","Abel"],"why":"Genesis 4:7."},{"q":"Who said, \"Am I my brother's keeper?\"","o":["Cain","Abel","Adam","God"],"why":"Genesis 4:9."}],"words":["CAIN","ABEL","SHEEP","ANGER","DOOR","GIFT"]},"gnA":{"passage":[[4,19,22],[5,18,27]],"intro":[{"sc":"field2","n":"After Cain, the world filled with people. Cain's family built the first city. Jubal invented the harp and flute. Tubal-cain was the first to work with bronze and iron."},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"Then came a man named Enoch. The Bible says something special about him: \"Enoch walked with God.\""},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"For 300 years, Enoch walked closely with God, every day. And then one day, he was gone. He didn't die. \"He was not, for God took him.\""},{"sc":"cosmos","n":"Enoch's son was Methuselah, who lived 969 years, the oldest person ever recorded in the Bible!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Walk with God every day","text":"Enoch's whole life is summed up in four words: 'He walked with God.' Not one big moment, but daily friendship for 300 years. Leaders build a daily walk with God, not just Sunday visits."},"order":["Cain's family builds the first city","Jubal invents musical instruments","Tubal-cain works with metal","Enoch walks with God for 300 years","God takes Enoch","Methuselah lives 969 years"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does the Bible say about Enoch?","o":["He walked with God","He built a tower","He was a king","He was a giant"],"why":"Genesis 5:24."},{"q":"What happened to Enoch?","o":["God took him, and he didn't die","He drowned","He went to Egypt","He became a king"],"why":"Genesis 5:24."},{"q":"Who lived the longest in the Bible?","o":["Methuselah, 969 years","Noah","Adam","Enoch"],"why":"Genesis 5:27."}],"words":["ENOCH","WALKED","METHUSELAH","JUBAL","HARP","IRON"]},"gn4":{"icon":"🌈","passage":[[6,9,22],[7,17,24],[8,1,12],[9,8,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"ark","n":"Years later, the whole world was full of violence and evil. But one man still walked with God: Noah."},{"sc":"arkbuild","n":"God told Noah to build a huge boat, an ark, on dry land. So Noah and his sons cut wood, hammered and built, day after day, for years."},{"sc":"arkbuild","w":"bnoah","e":"smile","t":"God said build it, so we build it. Even if everyone laughs, we will obey."},{"sc":"flood","n":"Then the rain came, for forty days and forty nights. The water covered even the mountains. But the ark floated safely."},{"sc":"rainbow","n":"When the water went down, Noah sent out a dove. It came back with an olive leaf! God put a rainbow in the sky as a promise."}],"lesson":{"title":"Do the right thing, even alone","text":"Noah was the only one who walked with God, and he built a boat on dry land while others probably laughed. He did everything God told him. Leaders obey God even when nobody else is doing it."},"order":["The world is full of evil","God tells Noah to build an ark","Noah, his family and the animals go in","It rains for forty days and nights","Noah sends out a dove","God puts a rainbow in the sky"],"quiz":[{"q":"What kind of man was Noah?","o":["He walked with God","He was a king","He was lazy","He was a fisherman"],"why":"Genesis 6:9."},{"q":"What did the dove bring back?","o":["An olive leaf","A fish","A flower","A stick"],"why":"A sign that the water was going down."},{"q":"What was the sign of God's promise?","o":["A rainbow","A star","A dove","A cloud"],"why":"Genesis 9:13."}],"words":["ARK","RAIN","DOVE","NOAH","RAINBOW","OLIVE"]},"gnB":{"passage":[[9,18,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"vineyard","n":"After the flood, Noah became a farmer and planted a vineyard. He made wine, drank too much, and fell asleep, uncovered, in his tent."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"His son Ham saw his father lying there, and went outside and made fun of him to his brothers."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"But his brothers Shem and Japheth took a cloak, walked in backwards so they wouldn't look, and gently covered their father."},{"sc":"vineyard","n":"When Noah woke up and found out, he blessed Shem and Japheth, and spoke a curse over Ham's son Canaan. Even heroes like Noah have weak moments."}],"lesson":{"title":"Cover, don't expose","text":"Noah made a mistake. Ham chose to mock and spread it; his brothers chose to protect their father's dignity. When people we respect fall, we can choose shame or kindness. Leaders cover others' weaknesses with respect instead of exposing them."},"order":["Noah plants a vineyard","Noah drinks too much wine","Ham mocks his father","Shem and Japheth walk in backwards","They cover their father","Noah blesses Shem and Japheth"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Noah plant after the flood?","o":["A vineyard","Wheat","Apple trees","A forest"],"why":"Genesis 9:20."},{"q":"How did Shem and Japheth cover their father?","o":["They walked in backwards so they wouldn't look","They shouted at him","They called Ham","They ran away"],"why":"Genesis 9:23."},{"q":"What is the lesson?","o":["Protect people's dignity instead of mocking their mistakes","Never plant grapes","Always sleep in tents","Mock your parents"],"why":"Cover, don't expose."}],"words":["NOAH","VINEYARD","SHEM","JAPHETH","HAM","CLOAK"]},"gn5":{"icon":"🏗️","passage":[[11,1,9]],"intro":[{"sc":"babel","n":"After the flood, Noah's sons' families spread out. One of them, Nimrod, became the first mighty warrior on earth, a famous hunter, who built cities in the land of Shinar, including Babel."},{"sc":"babel","n":"After the flood, everyone on earth spoke one language."},{"sc":"babel","n":"Some people said, \"Let's build a city, with a tower that reaches up to heaven, and make a great name for ourselves!\""},{"sc":"babel","n":"They wanted to be great without God. So God mixed up their language. Suddenly they couldn't understand each other!"},{"sc":"babel","n":"The building stopped, and the people spread out over the whole earth. The place was called Babel."}],"lesson":{"title":"Pride builds towers that fall","text":"The builders wanted to make a name for themselves. That's pride: wanting to be great without God. Leaders build things for God's glory and for others' good, not just to make themselves famous."},"order":["Everyone speaks one language","People decide to build a tall tower","They want to make a great name for themselves","God mixes up their language","The building stops","People spread over the whole earth"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did the people build the tower?","o":["To make a great name for themselves","To worship God","To escape a flood","To store food"],"why":"Genesis 11:4."},{"q":"What did God do to stop them?","o":["Mixed up their language","Sent a storm","Knocked the tower down with fire","Sent a lion"],"why":"They could no longer understand each other."},{"q":"\"Pride goes before ___.\"","o":["destruction","dinner","success","sleep"],"why":"Proverbs 16:18."}],"words":["TOWER","BRICK","PRIDE","BABEL","NAME","CITY"]},"gn6":{"icon":"⭐","passage":[[12,1,9],[15,1,6]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"In a city called Haran lived a man named Abram. One day, God spoke to him."},{"sc":"tents","n":"\"Leave your country, your family and your father's house, and go to a land I will show you. I will make you a great nation, and you will be a blessing.\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Abram didn't know where he was going. But he packed up and went, with his wife Sarai and his nephew Lot."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"One night God took Abram outside. \"Look at the stars. Can you count them? That's how many children you will have.\" Abram believed God."}],"lesson":{"title":"Faith takes the first step","text":"Abram didn't get a map. He got a promise. He believed God and went. And when it seemed impossible, he believed again. Leaders of faith take the first step before they can see the whole road."},"order":["God tells Abram to leave his country","Abram sets out with Sarai and Lot","Abram builds an altar to God in the new land","God tells Abram to look at the stars","Abram believes God"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did God ask Abram to do?","o":["Leave his country and go to a land God would show him","Build an ark","Build a tower","Go back home"],"why":"Genesis 12:1."},{"q":"What did God tell Abram to count?","o":["The stars","The sheep","The sand","The trees"],"why":"Genesis 15:5."},{"q":"What did Abram do when God made the promise?","o":["He believed God","He laughed","He ran away","He argued"],"why":"Genesis 15:6: \"he had faith in the Lord\"."}],"words":["ABRAM","STARS","FAITH","TENT","BLESS","JOURNEY"]},"gnC":{"passage":[[12,10,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Right after God's amazing promises, a famine came to the land. Abram went down to Egypt to find food."},{"sc":"egypt","w":"babraham","e":"worried","t":"Sarai, you're so beautiful. When the Egyptians see you, they'll kill me to take you. Tell them you're my sister, so they'll be kind to me."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"It was a half-truth: she was his half-sister, but she was also his wife. Pharaoh took Sarai into his palace, and gave Abram sheep, cattle, donkeys and camels."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"But God sent terrible sicknesses on Pharaoh's household. Pharaoh found out the truth and was furious. \"Why didn't you tell me she was your wife? Take her and go!\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Sadly, years later, Abraham told the same half-truth again to a king named Abimelech. And again, God protected Sarah."}],"lesson":{"title":"Fear makes even great people lie","text":"Abram had just trusted God enough to leave everything. Then fear made him lie, and put his wife in danger. God still protected them. Faith isn't a one-time thing. Leaders keep trusting God in new fears, instead of falling back on lies."},"order":["A famine comes to the land","Abram goes down to Egypt","Abram tells Sarai to say she's his sister","Pharaoh takes Sarai into his palace","God sends sickness on Pharaoh's house","Pharaoh sends Abram away"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Abram go to Egypt?","o":["There was a famine","To visit Pharaoh","To find gold","God told him to"],"why":"Genesis 12:10."},{"q":"What did Abram tell Sarai to say?","o":["That she was his sister","That she was a princess","That she was a servant","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 12:13."},{"q":"Who protected Sarai?","o":["God","Abram","Pharaoh","Lot"],"why":"Genesis 12:17."}],"words":["EGYPT","FAMINE","SARAI","SISTER","FEAR","TRUTH"]},"gnD":{"passage":[[13,1,18]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Abram and his nephew Lot both became very rich, with huge flocks and herds. There wasn't enough grass and water for everyone, and their herdsmen started fighting."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"babraham","e":"smile","t":"Let's not quarrel. We're family! The whole land is in front of you. You choose first. If you go left, I'll go right. If you go right, I'll go left."},{"sc":"jordan","n":"Lot looked around and saw the green, well-watered Jordan valley, like the garden of the Lord. He chose it, and moved his tents near the city of Sodom. But the men of Sodom were very wicked."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"After Lot left, God said to Abram: \"Look north, south, east and west. All the land you see, I will give to you and your children for ever. Walk through it!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Let others choose first","text":"Abram was the older one, and he had every right to choose. Instead, he made peace and let Lot pick. Lot chose what looked best, near a wicked city. Abram trusted God, and God gave him even more. Leaders put peace above being first."},"order":["Abram and Lot both become rich","Their herdsmen quarrel","Abram lets Lot choose first","Lot chooses the green Jordan valley","Lot moves near Sodom","God promises Abram all the land he can see"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Abram and Lot separate?","o":["There wasn't enough land for both of their flocks","They hated each other","God told Lot to leave","Lot was lost"],"why":"Genesis 13:6."},{"q":"Who chose first?","o":["Lot","Abram","Sarai","God"],"why":"Abram let Lot choose."},{"q":"Which city did Lot move near?","o":["Sodom","Jerusalem","Egypt","Babel"],"why":"Genesis 13:12."}],"words":["ABRAM","LOT","PEACE","CHOOSE","JORDAN","SODOM"]},"gnE":{"passage":[[14,11,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"battlehill","n":"Four kings went to war against five kings, including the king of Sodom. They captured Sodom and carried off all its people, including Lot!"},{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"When Abram heard, he gathered his 318 trained servants. They chased the kings all the way north, attacked at night, and rescued Lot and everyone else."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Then a mysterious man appeared: Melchizedek, king of Salem and priest of God Most High. He brought bread and wine, and blessed Abram."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bmelchi","e":"smile","t":"Blessed be Abram by God Most High, maker of heaven and earth! And blessed be God Most High, who gave your enemies into your hand!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"Abram gave him a tenth of everything. But when the king of Sodom offered Abram all the treasure, Abram refused: \"I won't take even a thread or a sandal strap, so you can never say, 'I made Abram rich.'\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Rescue, give, and refuse the wrong reward","text":"Abram risked everything to rescue Lot, gave a tenth to God's priest, and refused riches from a wicked king. Leaders rescue others, honour God with their gains, and won't take rewards that would make them owe the wrong people."},"order":["Four kings capture Sodom and Lot","Abram gathers 318 men","They rescue Lot at night","Melchizedek brings bread and wine","Abram gives him a tenth","Abram refuses Sodom's treasure"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many trained men did Abram take?","o":["318","12","1,000","40"],"why":"Genesis 14:14."},{"q":"What did Melchizedek bring?","o":["Bread and wine","Gold","A sword","A crown"],"why":"Genesis 14:18."},{"q":"What did Abram refuse from the king of Sodom?","o":["Even a thread or a sandal strap","Bread","His blessing","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 14:23."}],"words":["RESCUE","MELCHIZEDEK","BREAD","WINE","TENTH","SALEM"]},"gnF":{"passage":[[16,1,16]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Years passed, and Sarai still had no baby. She lost patience and came up with her own plan. She gave her Egyptian servant, Hagar, to Abram as a second wife, so Hagar could have a child for her."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Hagar became pregnant, and began to look down on Sarai. Sarai was furious and treated Hagar so harshly that Hagar ran away into the desert."},{"sc":"well","n":"By a spring in the wilderness, the angel of the Lord found her. \"Hagar, where have you come from, and where are you going?\""},{"sc":"well","n":"\"Go back. I will give you more descendants than you can count. Your son will be called Ishmael, 'God hears', because the Lord has heard your misery.\""},{"sc":"well","w":"bhagar","e":"big","t":"You are the God who sees me! I have seen the One who sees me!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God sees the overlooked","text":"Sarai's impatient plan caused pain for everyone, especially Hagar, a foreign servant with no power. But God went looking for her in the desert. She's the only person in the Bible who gave God a name: 'the God who sees me'. Nobody is invisible to God."},"order":["Sarai has no baby","Sarai gives Hagar to Abram","Hagar and Sarai quarrel","Hagar runs into the desert","The angel finds her by a spring","Hagar calls God 'the One who sees me'"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Hagar from?","o":["Egypt","Canaan","Babel","Moab"],"why":"Genesis 16:1."},{"q":"What does Ishmael mean?","o":["God hears","Laughter","Strong","Gift"],"why":"Genesis 16:11."},{"q":"What name did Hagar give God?","o":["The God who sees me","The Rock","The King","The Shepherd"],"why":"Genesis 16:13."}],"words":["HAGAR","DESERT","SPRING","ISHMAEL","SEES","HEARS"]},"gnG":{"passage":[[17,1,8],[17,15,22]],"intro":[{"sc":"starsky","n":"When Abram was 99 years old, God appeared to him: \"I am God Almighty. Walk with Me and be blameless.\""},{"sc":"starsky","n":"God gave him a new name. Abram, 'exalted father', became Abraham, 'father of many nations'. And Sarai became Sarah, 'princess'."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"God gave a sign of His covenant: every boy in Abraham's family would be circumcised, a special mark that they belonged to God."},{"sc":"starsky","w":"babraham","e":"big","t":"Ha! Will a son be born to a man who is a hundred, and to Sarah who is ninety?"},{"sc":"starsky","n":"God said, \"Yes! Sarah will have a son, and you'll name him Isaac. I'll keep my promise with him for ever. And I'll bless Ishmael too.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"God names you by your future","text":"Abraham had no children with Sarah, but God called him 'father of many nations'. God sees who you're becoming, not just who you are today. Leaders believe what God says about them, even before it's visible."},"order":["God appears to 99-year-old Abram","Abram becomes Abraham","Sarai becomes Sarah","God gives the sign of the covenant","Abraham laughs","God says the son will be called Isaac"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does Abraham mean?","o":["Father of many nations","Rich man","Old man","Friend"],"why":"Genesis 17:5."},{"q":"What was Sarai's new name?","o":["Sarah","Rebekah","Rachel","Leah"],"why":"Genesis 17:15."},{"q":"How old was Abraham?","o":["99","40","75","120"],"why":"Genesis 17:1."}],"words":["ABRAHAM","SARAH","NAMES","COVENANT","NATIONS","ALMIGHTY"]},"gn7":{"icon":"😄","passage":[[18,1,15],[21,1,7]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Years passed. Abraham and Sarah (God had given them new names) were very old, and still had no children."},{"sc":"tents","n":"One hot day, three visitors came to Abraham's tent. He ran to welcome them and made them a big meal."},{"sc":"tents","n":"One said, \"By this time next year, Sarah will have a son.\" Sarah, listening inside the tent, laughed to herself. She was ninety years old!"},{"sc":"tents","w":"bsarah","e":"big","t":"God has given me cause for laughing, and everyone who hears about it will laugh with me!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"But God kept His promise. Sarah had a baby boy, and named him Isaac, which means 'he laughs'. Now she laughed for joy!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Nothing is too hard for God","text":"Sarah laughed because it seemed impossible. God asked, \"Is anything too hard for the Lord?\" Then He did it. Leaders remember that God's promises don't depend on what looks possible."},"order":["Three visitors come to Abraham's tent","Abraham makes them a meal","A visitor says Sarah will have a son","Sarah laughs to herself","Isaac is born","Sarah laughs with joy"],"quiz":[{"q":"How old was Sarah when Isaac was born?","o":["About ninety","Twenty","Forty","Twelve"],"why":"Far too old, except for God!"},{"q":"What does the name Isaac mean?","o":["He laughs","He runs","Star","Gift"],"why":"Sarah laughed, first in doubt, then in joy."},{"q":"Who said, \"God has given me cause for laughing\"?","o":["Sarah","Abraham","Isaac","The visitor"],"why":"Genesis 21:6."}],"words":["SARAH","ISAAC","LAUGH","TENT","PROMISE","BABY"]},"gnH":{"passage":[[18,16,33]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"After the visit to Abraham's tent, the Lord told Abraham that the cries against Sodom were so great, He was going to see whether to destroy it. Abraham's nephew Lot lived there!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"babraham","e":"worried","t":"Will You sweep away the good people with the wicked? What if there are fifty good people in the city? Shall not the Judge of all the earth do what is right?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"God said, \"For fifty good people, I will spare the whole city.\""},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"babraham","e":"worried","t":"What if there are only forty-five? ...Forty? ...Thirty? ...Twenty? Please don't be angry. Just once more: what if there are only ten?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"God said, \"For the sake of ten, I will not destroy it.\" Abraham had asked boldly, humbly, and over and over, for the people of a wicked city."}],"lesson":{"title":"Pray boldly for others","text":"Abraham didn't pray for himself. He pleaded again and again for a city full of wicked people, and God patiently listened every time. Leaders stand in the gap and pray boldly for others, even people who don't deserve it."},"order":["God tells Abraham about Sodom","Abraham asks about fifty good people","God agrees to spare it for fifty","Abraham asks for forty-five, forty, thirty, twenty","Abraham asks about ten","God agrees to spare it for ten"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many good people did Abraham start with?","o":["Fifty","Ten","One hundred","Five"],"why":"Genesis 18:24."},{"q":"Where did he stop?","o":["Ten","Twenty","One","Forty"],"why":"Genesis 18:32."},{"q":"What did Abraham ask about the Judge of all the earth?","o":["Shall He not do what is right?","Is He angry?","Where is He?","Is He tired?"],"why":"Genesis 18:25."}],"words":["SODOM","PRAY","FIFTY","TEN","JUDGE","BOLD"]},"gnI":{"passage":[[19,1,3],[19,12,29]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"Two angels arrived at Sodom in the evening. Lot was sitting at the city gate, and he insisted they stay at his house for safety."},{"sc":"townnight","n":"That night, the wicked men of the city surrounded Lot's house and demanded he hand over his guests to hurt them. The angels struck the mob blind so they couldn't even find the door!"},{"sc":"townnight","n":"\"Get your family out of here! The Lord is about to destroy this city.\" Lot's daughters' fiancés thought he was joking. Even Lot hesitated."},{"sc":"sodom","n":"At dawn, the angels grabbed Lot, his wife and two daughters by the hand and pulled them out, because the Lord was merciful. \"Run for your lives! Don't look back!\""},{"sc":"sodom","n":"Then fire and burning sulphur rained down on Sodom and Gomorrah. But Lot's wife looked back towards the city she loved, and she became a pillar of salt."},{"sc":"sodom","n":"Lot's family had lived among wickedness so long that it had shaped them. Even after they escaped, his daughters later did something shameful. The family started in Sodom, and Sodom never really left them."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't look back","text":"Lot hesitated. His wife longed for what she was leaving. When God rescues us from something harmful, we have to really leave it behind. Jesus said: 'Remember Lot's wife.' Leaders don't keep looking back at what God has called them out of."},"order":["Two angels arrive in Sodom","Lot takes them into his house","The mob is struck blind","The angels pull the family out","Fire falls on Sodom","Lot's wife looks back"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was Lot sitting when the angels came?","o":["At the city gate","In the field","On the roof","In the temple"],"why":"Genesis 19:1."},{"q":"What happened to the wicked mob?","o":["They were struck blind","They ran away","They became angels","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 19:11."},{"q":"What happened to Lot's wife?","o":["She became a pillar of salt","She ran ahead","She stayed in Sodom","She became a queen"],"why":"Genesis 19:26."}],"words":["SODOM","ANGELS","FIRE","SALT","LOOK","MERCY"]},"gnJ":{"passage":[[21,8,21]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"At the feast for little Isaac, Sarah saw Ishmael, now a teenager, mocking her son. She told Abraham, \"Send that servant and her son away!\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Abraham was very upset; Ishmael was his son too. But God said, \"Do what Sarah says. I will make Ishmael into a nation as well.\""},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Early in the morning, Abraham gave Hagar bread and a skin of water, and sent them away. They wandered in the desert until the water ran out."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Hagar put the boy under a bush and sat far away. \"I can't watch my son die.\" And she cried."},{"sc":"well","n":"God heard the boy crying. The angel called: \"Don't be afraid, Hagar. God has heard the boy. Lift him up!\" Then God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of water."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"God was with the boy as he grew up in the desert. Ishmael became a skilled archer."}],"lesson":{"title":"God hears the cries of the rejected","text":"Hagar and Ishmael were sent away, alone and helpless. But the God who 'sees' also 'hears'. He heard a crying boy under a bush, and opened a mother's eyes to the answer right in front of her. Leaders notice people who've been pushed out, because God does."},"order":["Ishmael mocks Isaac at the feast","Sarah tells Abraham to send them away","Abraham gives them bread and water","Their water runs out","God hears the boy crying","God shows Hagar a well"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Abraham give Hagar?","o":["Bread and a skin of water","Gold","A camel","A tent"],"why":"Genesis 21:14."},{"q":"Whose cry did God hear?","o":["The boy's","Sarah's","Abraham's","A bird's"],"why":"Genesis 21:17."},{"q":"What did God show Hagar?","o":["A well of water","A city","A camel","A tent"],"why":"Genesis 21:19."}],"words":["HAGAR","ISHMAEL","DESERT","WELL","CRY","ARCHER"]},"gn8":{"icon":"🐏","passage":[[22,1,19]],"intro":[{"sc":"mountain","n":"When Isaac was a boy, God gave Abraham the hardest test of his life."},{"sc":"mountain","n":"God told Abraham to take Isaac up Mount Moriah and offer him as a sacrifice. Abraham was heartbroken, but he trusted God."},{"sc":"mountain","w":"bisaac","e":"worried","t":"My father, we have wood and fire here, but where is the lamb?"},{"sc":"mountain","w":"babraham","e":"smile","t":"God himself will give the lamb."},{"sc":"mountain","n":"At the last moment, an angel stopped Abraham! There was a ram caught in a bush. God had provided a sacrifice in Isaac's place."}],"lesson":{"title":"Trust God with what you love most","text":"Abraham loved Isaac more than anything, but he trusted God even more. And God provided. Many years later, God gave His own Son, Jesus, as the Lamb in our place. Leaders hold everything with open hands, trusting God to provide."},"order":["God tests Abraham","Abraham and Isaac climb Mount Moriah","Isaac asks, \"Where is the lamb?\"","An angel stops Abraham","Abraham sees a ram caught in a bush","God blesses Abraham again"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which mountain did Abraham and Isaac climb?","o":["Mount Moriah","Mount Sinai","Mount Everest","Mount Ararat"],"why":"Genesis 22:2."},{"q":"What did Isaac ask his father?","o":["\"Where is the lamb?\"","\"Where is the tent?\"","\"Are we lost?\"","\"Can we go home?\""],"why":"Genesis 22:7."},{"q":"What did God provide in Isaac's place?","o":["A ram caught in a bush","A lion","A dove","A goat"],"why":"God himself provided."}],"words":["ISAAC","RAM","ALTAR","TRUST","ANGEL","LAMB"]},"gnK":{"passage":[[23,1,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Sarah lived to be 127 years old, and died at Hebron. Abraham mourned and wept for her."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Abraham owned no land of his own in Canaan yet. He went to the Hittites at the city gate and asked to buy a burial place: the cave of Machpelah."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"The owner, Ephron, said politely, \"I give it to you!\" But Abraham insisted on paying the full price: 400 shekels of silver, weighed out in front of everyone."},{"sc":"cave","n":"Abraham buried Sarah in the cave. It was the first piece of the promised land his family ever owned. Later Abraham, Isaac, Rebekah, Jacob and Leah were all buried there too."}],"lesson":{"title":"Honour, and do things properly","text":"Even in grief, Abraham acted with honour. He paid the full price openly, so nobody could ever question his family's claim. Leaders do business honestly and publicly, even in hard times."},"order":["Sarah dies at age 127","Abraham weeps for her","Abraham asks to buy a burial place","Ephron offers it for free","Abraham insists on paying","Sarah is buried in the cave of Machpelah"],"quiz":[{"q":"How old was Sarah when she died?","o":["127","90","100","175"],"why":"Genesis 23:1."},{"q":"What was the cave called?","o":["Machpelah","Adullam","Bethel","Moriah"],"why":"Genesis 23:9."},{"q":"Why did Abraham insist on paying?","o":["So the land would truly and openly belong to his family","He was rich","Ephron was angry","He had to"],"why":"Doing things properly."}],"words":["SARAH","CAVE","MACHPELAH","SILVER","HONOUR","HEBRON"]},"gnL":{"passage":[[24,10,27],[24,57,67]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Abraham was old. He sent his most trusted servant on a long journey back to his homeland, with ten camels, to find a wife for Isaac."},{"sc":"well","n":"The servant arrived at a well outside the town in the evening, when the women came to draw water. He prayed a very specific prayer."},{"sc":"well","w":"beliezer","e":"worried","t":"Lord, the girl I ask for a drink, if she says, 'Drink, and I'll water your camels too,' let her be the one You've chosen for Isaac."},{"sc":"well","n":"Before he had even finished praying, a beautiful young woman named Rebekah came out with a jar on her shoulder."},{"sc":"well","w":"brebekah","e":"smile","t":"Drink, my lord! And I'll draw water for your camels too, until they've finished drinking!"},{"sc":"well","n":"Ten thirsty camels can drink a LOT of water! The servant bowed and worshipped God. Rebekah agreed to go with him, and when Isaac met her, he loved her."}],"lesson":{"title":"Kindness beyond what's asked","text":"Rebekah only had to give a stranger a drink. She chose to water ten thirsty camels too, hard work, with no reward expected. And the servant prayed before he searched. Leaders pray for guidance, and they do more than what's required."},"order":["Abraham sends his servant to find a wife for Isaac","The servant arrives at a well","He prays a specific prayer","Rebekah arrives before he finishes","Rebekah waters all his camels","Isaac marries Rebekah"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many camels did the servant bring?","o":["Ten","Two","One hundred","Forty"],"why":"Genesis 24:10."},{"q":"When did Rebekah appear?","o":["Before he had finished praying","The next day","A week later","Never"],"why":"Genesis 24:15."},{"q":"What did Rebekah offer to do?","o":["Water all his camels too","Sell him water","Show him the city","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 24:19."}],"words":["REBEKAH","WELL","CAMELS","PRAYER","WATER","ISAAC"]},"gn9":{"icon":"🍲","passage":[[25,27,34],[27,1,29]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Isaac and Rebekah had twin boys. Esau was a hairy hunter who loved the outdoors. Jacob was quiet, and stayed near the tents."},{"sc":"tents","w":"besau","e":"worried","t":"I'm starving! Give me some of that red soup!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"One day Esau came home starving. Jacob was cooking red soup. \"Give me some!\" \"Only if you give me your birthright.\" Esau agreed, for one bowl of soup!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"Years later, old blind Isaac wanted to bless Esau. But Rebekah helped Jacob dress like Esau, with goat skins on his arms."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bisaacold","e":"worried","t":"The voice is Jacob's voice, but the hands are the hands of Esau."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Isaac was tricked, and gave the blessing to Jacob."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't trade the precious for the instant","text":"Esau swapped something precious for something he wanted right now. Jacob got what he wanted by lying. Both choices caused years of pain. Leaders value what really matters, and they never get ahead by deceiving people."},"order":["Twins Esau and Jacob are born","Esau comes home starving","Esau sells his birthright for soup","Rebekah helps Jacob dress like Esau","Isaac blesses Jacob by mistake"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Esau trade his birthright for?","o":["A bowl of soup","A camel","Gold","A coat"],"why":"Genesis 25:34."},{"q":"How did Jacob trick his father?","o":["He dressed up like Esau, with goat skins on his arms","He hid","He sang a song","He wrote a letter"],"why":"Genesis 27."},{"q":"Who said, \"The voice is Jacob's voice, but the hands are the hands of Esau\"?","o":["Isaac","Rebekah","Esau","Jacob"],"why":"Genesis 27:22."}],"words":["ESAU","JACOB","SOUP","TWINS","HUNTER","BLESS"]},"gnM":{"passage":[[26,12,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"ploughfield","n":"God blessed Isaac's farming so much that he harvested a hundred times what he planted! The Philistines became jealous and filled his father's old wells with dirt."},{"sc":"well","n":"Isaac's servants dug a new well and found fresh water. But the local herdsmen said, \"That's our water!\" Isaac didn't fight. He moved on and called it Esek, 'arguing'."},{"sc":"well","n":"They dug another well, and there was another quarrel. He called it Sitnah, 'enemy', and moved on again."},{"sc":"well","n":"They dug a third well, and nobody argued. Isaac called it Rehoboth, 'room': \"Now the Lord has made room for us!\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Later, the Philistine king came to make peace: \"We can see the Lord is with you.\" That same day, Isaac's servants found water again."}],"lesson":{"title":"Make peace, and keep digging","text":"Isaac could have fought for every well. Instead, he kept moving and kept digging, until God made room. His peacefulness eventually won over his enemies. Leaders don't fight every battle; they trust God to make room."},"order":["Isaac's crops grow a hundred times","The Philistines fill in his wells","Herdsmen quarrel over a new well","Isaac moves on again","Rehoboth: no quarrel","The Philistine king makes peace"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does Rehoboth mean?","o":["Room","Arguing","Enemy","Water"],"why":"Genesis 26:22."},{"q":"What did Isaac do when people fought over his wells?","o":["Moved on and dug another","Fought them","Gave up","Moved to Egypt"],"why":"Genesis 26:21-22."},{"q":"Why did the Philistine king make peace?","o":["He saw the Lord was with Isaac","He was scared of Isaac's army","He wanted water","Isaac paid him"],"why":"Genesis 26:28."}],"words":["ISAAC","WELLS","DIG","REHOBOTH","ROOM","PEACE"]},"gn10":{"icon":"🪜","passage":[[28,10,22],[32,22,32]],"intro":[{"sc":"ladder","n":"Esau was furious, so Jacob ran away from home. That night, alone, he slept outside with a stone for a pillow."},{"sc":"ladder","n":"He dreamed of a stairway reaching from earth to heaven, with angels going up and down. And God promised, \"I will be with you wherever you go.\""},{"sc":"ladder","n":"Jacob woke up and said, \"Truly, the Lord is in this place, and I didn't know it!\""},{"sc":"ladder","w":"bjacob","e":"shock","t":"Truly, the Lord is in this place, and I didn't know it!"},{"sc":"river","n":"Twenty years later, on his way home, Jacob wrestled all night with a mysterious man. \"I won't let you go until you bless me!\" God changed his name to Israel."}],"lesson":{"title":"God doesn't give up on you","text":"Jacob was a trickster on the run, but God met him in the middle of nowhere with a promise. Later God changed his name, and his character. Leaders know their past mistakes don't stop God from working in them, if they hold on to Him."},"order":["Jacob runs away from Esau","Jacob sleeps with a stone for a pillow","Jacob dreams of a stairway to heaven","God promises to be with him","Jacob wrestles all night","God changes his name to Israel"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jacob see in his dream?","o":["A stairway with angels going up and down","A burning bush","A rainbow","A tower"],"why":"Genesis 28:12."},{"q":"What did Jacob say when he woke up?","o":["\"Truly, the Lord is in this place and I was not conscious of it\"","\"I'm hungry\"","\"Where is Esau?\"","\"I want to go home\""],"why":"Genesis 28:16."},{"q":"What new name did God give Jacob?","o":["Israel","Abraham","Joseph","Isaac"],"why":"Genesis 32:28."}],"words":["LADDER","DREAM","ANGELS","STONE","ISRAEL","WRESTLE"]},"gnN":{"passage":[[29,9,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"well","n":"Jacob, running from Esau, reached a well in the east. A shepherdess came with her father's sheep: Rachel. Jacob rolled the heavy stone from the well, watered her sheep, kissed her, and wept for joy."},{"sc":"flock","n":"He stayed with her father, his uncle Laban. \"I'll work seven years for Rachel.\" Because he loved her so much, the seven years seemed like just a few days!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"At the wedding feast, Laban secretly sent in his older daughter, Leah, wearing a veil. In the morning, Jacob discovered he had married the wrong sister!"},{"sc":"tents","w":"bjacob","e":"shock","t":"What have you done to me? I worked for Rachel! Why did you trick me?"},{"sc":"tents","w":"blaban","e":"smirk","t":"Here, we don't give the younger daughter before the older. Work another seven years, and you can have Rachel too."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Jacob, who had tricked his own father, had now been tricked himself. He worked fourteen years in all."}],"lesson":{"title":"You reap what you sow","text":"Jacob had disguised himself to trick his blind father. Now someone used a disguise to trick him. Life often teaches us how our wrongs feel from the other side. Leaders learn from these lessons, and treat others the way they'd want to be treated."},"order":["Jacob meets Rachel at a well","He waters her sheep","He works seven years for her","Laban gives him Leah instead","Jacob discovers the trick","Jacob works seven more years"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jacob meet Rachel?","o":["At a well","In a palace","In the market","In Egypt"],"why":"Genesis 29:9-10."},{"q":"How did the first seven years feel?","o":["Like just a few days, because he loved her","Like forever","Boring","Scary"],"why":"Genesis 29:20."},{"q":"Who did Laban give Jacob first?","o":["Leah","Rachel","Rebekah","Dinah"],"why":"Genesis 29:23."}],"words":["RACHEL","LEAH","LABAN","SEVEN","TRICKED","WEDDING"]},"gnO":{"passage":[[29,31,35],[30,25,43]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Jacob loved Rachel more than Leah. But God saw that Leah was unloved, and gave her children. With each son, she hoped Jacob would love her."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bleah","e":"smile","t":"This time I will praise the Lord!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"She named that son Judah, meaning 'praise'. The sisters became rivals, competing over who had more children. In the end, Jacob had twelve sons and a daughter, and Rachel finally had Joseph."},{"sc":"flock","n":"Laban kept cheating Jacob, changing his wages ten times. So they agreed: Jacob could keep every speckled, spotted or dark animal born in the flock."},{"sc":"flock","n":"Jacob tried a strange trick with peeled, striped sticks by the water troughs. But later he admitted the real reason the flock produced so many spotted animals: \"God has taken your father's animals and given them to me.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"God sees the unloved","text":"Leah was the sister nobody chose first. But God saw her, and from her son Judah would come King David, and Jesus. When she stopped trying to win Jacob's love and praised God instead, something changed. Leaders find their worth in God, not in winning others' approval."},"order":["Jacob loves Rachel more than Leah","God gives Leah sons","Leah names Judah and praises God","Rachel finally has Joseph","Laban changes Jacob's wages","God blesses Jacob's spotted flock"],"quiz":[{"q":"What does Judah mean?","o":["Praise","Laughter","Strong","Seen"],"why":"Genesis 29:35."},{"q":"Which animals could Jacob keep?","o":["The speckled, spotted and dark ones","The biggest","The white ones","None"],"why":"Genesis 30:32."},{"q":"Who did Jacob say really gave him the animals?","o":["God","Laban","Rachel","The sticks"],"why":"Genesis 31:9."}],"words":["LEAH","JUDAH","PRAISE","SPOTTED","STICKS","FLOCK"]},"gnP":{"passage":[[31,17,24],[31,30,35],[31,44,49]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"God told Jacob, \"Go home.\" So while Laban was away shearing sheep, Jacob secretly packed up his family and flocks and left. And Rachel secretly stole her father's household idols!"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Laban chased them for seven days. But God warned Laban in a dream: \"Be careful. Don't say anything to Jacob, good or bad.\""},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"blaban","e":"frown","t":"Why did you sneak away? And why did you steal my gods?"},{"sc":"tents","n":"Jacob had no idea Rachel had taken them. \"Search everything!\" Laban searched every tent. Rachel had hidden the idols in her camel's saddle, and she was sitting on it!"},{"sc":"tents","w":"brachel","e":"worried","t":"Don't be angry, father. I can't get up for you right now. I'm not feeling well."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Laban found nothing. In the end, he and Jacob made peace and piled up stones as a witness. Laban called it Mizpah: \"May the Lord watch between you and me when we're apart.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Family drama, and God's protection","text":"This family was full of tricks: Laban cheated, Jacob ran secretly, and Rachel stole and lied. Yet God protected them and brought peace. God works even in messy families. Leaders aim for honest peace instead of hidden tricks."},"order":["God tells Jacob to go home","Jacob leaves secretly","Rachel steals her father's idols","Laban chases them","Rachel hides the idols under her saddle","Laban and Jacob make peace at Mizpah"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Rachel steal?","o":["Her father's household idols","Gold","A sheep","A camel"],"why":"Genesis 31:19."},{"q":"Where did she hide them?","o":["In her camel's saddle, and sat on it","In a well","In a tree","Under a rock"],"why":"Genesis 31:34."},{"q":"What does Mizpah ask?","o":["May the Lord watch between us when we're apart","Go away","Where are my gods?","Let's fight"],"why":"Genesis 31:49."}],"words":["RACHEL","IDOLS","SADDLE","LABAN","MIZPAH","PEACE"]},"gnQ":{"passage":[[32,3,12],[33,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Jacob heard that Esau was coming to meet him, with 400 men! Twenty years earlier, Esau had wanted to kill him. Jacob was terrified."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bjacob","e":"worried","t":"O God, I'm not worthy of all Your kindness. Save me from my brother Esau, I'm afraid he will attack us!"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Jacob sent gift after gift ahead of him: goats, sheep, camels, cows and donkeys, hundreds of animals, hoping to calm Esau down."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"Then Jacob went ahead of his family, bowing to the ground seven times as he came near his brother."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"But Esau RAN to meet him. He threw his arms around his neck, kissed him, and they both wept!"},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"bjacob","e":"big","t":"Seeing your face is like seeing the face of God, now that you've welcomed me!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Make it right","text":"Jacob had wronged his brother badly. Instead of avoiding Esau for ever, he humbly went to meet him, ready to make it right. And Esau surprised everyone with forgiveness. Leaders face the people they've hurt, and they're quick to forgive when others come back."},"order":["Jacob hears Esau is coming with 400 men","Jacob prays in fear","Jacob sends gifts ahead","Jacob bows seven times","Esau runs and hugs him","They both weep"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many men came with Esau?","o":["400","12","40","1,000"],"why":"Genesis 32:6."},{"q":"How many times did Jacob bow?","o":["Seven","Once","Three","Ten"],"why":"Genesis 33:3."},{"q":"What did Esau do?","o":["Ran, hugged and kissed him","Attacked him","Ignored him","Took his gifts and left"],"why":"Genesis 33:4."}],"words":["ESAU","JACOB","HUG","GIFTS","FORGIVE","WEEP"]},"gnR":{"passage":[[34,1,7],[34,25,31]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"Jacob's daughter Dinah went out to visit the young women of the land. Shechem, the prince of that city, took her and violated her. Then he wanted to marry her."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Dinah's brothers were furious. They pretended to agree to a peace deal, but only if every man in the city was circumcised."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Three days later, while the men were still in pain, two brothers, Simeon and Levi, attacked the city with swords. They killed every man and took everything."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bjacob","e":"frown","t":"You've brought trouble on me! Now everyone around here will hate us!"},{"sc":"tents","n":"Years later, on his deathbed, Jacob still remembered: \"Simeon and Levi... cursed be their anger, for it was fierce, and their fury, for it was cruel.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Wrong is wrong, and so is revenge","text":"What happened to Dinah was a terrible wrong. But her brothers answered with deception and a massacre of innocent people. Anger at injustice is right; cruel revenge is not. Leaders seek justice, not revenge. And if anyone ever hurts you, tell a trusted adult."},"order":["Dinah visits the women of the land","Shechem violates Dinah","Her brothers make a false peace deal","Simeon and Levi attack the city","Jacob says they've brought trouble","Jacob never forgets their cruel anger"],"quiz":[{"q":"Was what happened to Dinah her fault?","o":["No, a terrible wrong was done to her","Yes","Partly","Nobody knows"],"why":"She was a victim."},{"q":"Which brothers attacked the city?","o":["Simeon and Levi","Judah and Joseph","Reuben and Benjamin","All twelve"],"why":"Genesis 34:25."},{"q":"What did Jacob say about their anger later?","o":["It was fierce and cruel","It was brave","It was right","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 49:7."}],"words":["DINAH","SIMEON","LEVI","REVENGE","JUSTICE","ANGER"]},"gnS":{"passage":[[35,1,7],[35,16,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","w":"bjacob","e":"stern","t":"Get rid of all the foreign gods you have! We're going to Bethel, where God answered me when I was in trouble."},{"sc":"ladder","n":"His family handed over their idols and earrings, and Jacob buried them under an oak tree. At Bethel, God appeared to him again and confirmed his new name: Israel."},{"sc":"tents","n":"As they travelled on towards Bethlehem, Rachel went into hard labour. She gave birth to a son, but she was dying."},{"sc":"tents","n":"With her last breath, she named him Ben-oni, 'son of my sorrow'. But Jacob renamed him Benjamin, 'son of my right hand'."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Rachel was buried on the road to Bethlehem, and Jacob set up a pillar on her grave. Jacob now had his twelfth and youngest son."}],"lesson":{"title":"Turning sorrow into strength","text":"Jacob first cleared out the idols so his family could start fresh with God. Then, in deep grief, he renamed his son from 'sorrow' to 'strength'. Leaders clear away what pulls their family from God, and they help turn sorrow into hope."},"order":["Jacob tells his family to get rid of idols","He buries them under an oak","God appears at Bethel again","Rachel gives birth on the road","She names him Ben-oni","Jacob renames him Benjamin"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jacob bury under the oak tree?","o":["The family's idols","Gold","Rachel","His staff"],"why":"Genesis 35:4."},{"q":"What did Rachel name her son?","o":["Ben-oni, 'son of my sorrow'","Joseph","Judah","Isaac"],"why":"Genesis 35:18."},{"q":"What does Benjamin mean?","o":["Son of my right hand","Sorrow","Laughter","Gift"],"why":"Genesis 35:18."}],"words":["BETHEL","IDOLS","RACHEL","BENJAMIN","SORROW","ISRAEL"]},"gn11":{"icon":"🧥","passage":[[37,1,36]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Jacob (Israel) had twelve sons. His favourite was Joseph, and he gave him a beautiful long coat. His brothers were jealous."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"Joseph had dreams that one day his whole family would bow down to him. When he told his brothers, they hated him even more."},{"sc":"pit","n":"One day the brothers saw Joseph coming. \"Here comes this dreamer!\" They threw him into a dry pit, then sold him to traders going to Egypt."},{"sc":"pit","n":"They dipped his coat in goat's blood and showed it to their father. Jacob thought a wild animal had killed Joseph, and he cried for days."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jealousy destroys families","text":"Favouritism and jealousy tore Joseph's family apart. The brothers let envy grow until they did something terrible. Leaders notice jealousy in their own hearts and deal with it early, and they treat people fairly."},"order":["Jacob gives Joseph a special coat","Joseph tells his brothers his dreams","The brothers say, \"Here comes this dreamer\"","They throw Joseph into a pit","They sell Joseph to traders","Jacob is told Joseph is dead"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jacob give Joseph?","o":["A long, special coat","A sword","A camel","A crown"],"why":"Genesis 37:3."},{"q":"Why did the brothers hate Joseph?","o":["Their father loved him most, and he told them his dreams","He was rude","He stole from them","He was lazy"],"why":"Favouritism and envy."},{"q":"Where did the traders take Joseph?","o":["Egypt","Babel","Canaan","Eden"],"why":"He was sold as a slave."}],"words":["JOSEPH","COAT","DREAM","PIT","EGYPT","BROTHERS"]},"gnT":{"passage":[[38,6,11],[38,24,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"While Joseph was a slave in Egypt, his brother Judah moved away and had a family. His oldest son married a woman named Tamar, but he was wicked and died."},{"sc":"tents","n":"By the law of that time, Judah's next son should have given Tamar a family. He refused. He died too. Judah promised his youngest son, Shelah, when he grew up... but he never kept his promise."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Tamar was left a widow with no future. So she made a bold, risky plan. She disguised herself, and Judah, not recognising her, slept with her. She asked for his seal, cord and staff as a pledge."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Months later, Judah heard Tamar was pregnant, and he was ready to have her punished! Tamar sent him his own seal, cord and staff: \"The man who owns these is the father.\""},{"sc":"tents","w":"bjudah","e":"worried","t":"She is more righteous than I am, because I didn't keep my promise to her."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Tamar had twins, Perez and Zerah. And Perez became an ancestor of King David, and of Jesus."}],"lesson":{"title":"Admit when you're wrong","text":"Judah broke his promise, treated Tamar unfairly, and was quick to judge her. But when the truth came out, he said, 'She is more righteous than I.' That was the start of Judah becoming a changed man. Leaders admit their wrongs openly, even when it's embarrassing."},"order":["Tamar's husband dies","Judah's second son refuses her","Judah breaks his promise","Tamar makes a bold plan","Judah is ready to punish her","Judah admits, \"She is more righteous than I\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What promise did Judah break?","o":["To give Tamar his son Shelah","To pay her","To build a house","To visit Joseph"],"why":"Genesis 38:11-14."},{"q":"What did Tamar show to prove the truth?","o":["Judah's seal, cord and staff","A letter","A coin","A ring"],"why":"Genesis 38:25."},{"q":"What did Judah say?","o":["\"She is more righteous than I\"","\"Punish her\"","\"I don't know her\"","Nothing"],"why":"Genesis 38:26."}],"words":["JUDAH","TAMAR","PROMISE","STAFF","SEAL","PEREZ"]},"gn12":{"icon":"👑","passage":[[39,1,6],[39,20,23],[40,1,23],[41,14,16],[41,25,43]],"intro":[{"sc":"egypt","n":"In Egypt, Joseph became a slave in the house of Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh. God was with Joseph, and everything he did went well."},{"sc":"prison","n":"But Potiphar's wife told lies about him, and Joseph was thrown into prison for something he didn't do. Even there, God was with him."},{"sc":"prison","n":"In prison, Joseph explained the dreams of Pharaoh's cup-bearer and baker. \"Remember me!\" he said. But the cup-bearer forgot him for two whole years."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Then Pharaoh had strange dreams nobody could explain. Joseph was brought from prison. God showed him the meaning, and Pharaoh made Joseph ruler over all Egypt!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Stay faithful when life is unfair","text":"Joseph was betrayed, lied about, and forgotten. But he kept doing his best, kept honouring God, and kept helping others, even in prison. Leaders stay faithful in the hidden, unfair seasons. God sees, and He lifts up in His time."},"order":["Joseph works in Potiphar's house","Joseph is thrown into prison unfairly","Joseph explains two prisoners' dreams","The cup-bearer forgets Joseph","Pharaoh has strange dreams","Joseph becomes ruler over Egypt"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why was Joseph put in prison?","o":["Potiphar's wife told lies about him","He stole","He was lazy","He ran away"],"why":"He was innocent."},{"q":"Who said, \"Does not the sense of dreams come from God?\"","o":["Joseph","Pharaoh","The baker","Potiphar"],"why":"Genesis 40:8. Joseph gave God the credit."},{"q":"What did Pharaoh make Joseph?","o":["Ruler over all Egypt","His cook","A soldier","A prisoner again"],"why":"From the prison to the palace."}],"words":["PRISON","PHARAOH","DREAMS","PALACE","RULER","FAITHFUL"]},"gnU":{"passage":[[42,6,9],[42,21,24],[44,1,13],[44,18,34]],"intro":[{"sc":"egypt","n":"When Joseph's brothers came to buy grain, they bowed to him, not recognising him. Joseph recognised them! He spoke harshly through an interpreter: \"You're spies!\""},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Among themselves, the brothers said, \"We're being punished for what we did to Joseph.\" They didn't know he understood every word. Joseph turned away and cried. He kept Simeon in prison and sent the others home with grain, and secretly put their money back in their sacks."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"When they returned with young Benjamin, Joseph gave them a feast. Then he secretly hid his own silver cup in Benjamin's sack!"},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Joseph's steward chased them: \"Who stole my master's cup?\" The sacks were opened, one by one... and the cup was in Benjamin's! The brothers tore their clothes in horror."},{"sc":"egypt","w":"bjudah","e":"worried","t":"Please, my lord, let me stay as your slave instead of the boy. If he doesn't come home, our father will die of sorrow. How can I go back without him?"},{"sc":"egypt","n":"The brother who once sold Joseph as a slave now offered to become a slave himself to save his little brother. Joseph couldn't hold back his tears any longer."}],"lesson":{"title":"People can change","text":"Joseph tested his brothers to see if they had changed. Years before, Judah had sold one brother into slavery. Now he offered his own freedom to save another. Leaders believe people can change, and they prove their own change with sacrifice."},"order":["The brothers bow to Joseph","Joseph calls them spies","Simeon is kept in prison","Joseph hides his silver cup in Benjamin's sack","The cup is found","Judah offers himself instead of Benjamin"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where was the silver cup found?","o":["In Benjamin's sack","In Judah's sack","In Joseph's palace","In the river"],"why":"Genesis 44:12."},{"q":"Which brother was kept in prison?","o":["Simeon","Benjamin","Reuben","Judah"],"why":"Genesis 42:24."},{"q":"What did Judah offer?","o":["To be a slave instead of Benjamin","Gold","To run away","To fight Joseph"],"why":"Genesis 44:33."}],"words":["SILVER","CUP","BENJAMIN","JUDAH","SACK","CHANGED"]},"gn13":{"icon":"🤗","passage":[[45,1,15],[50,15,21]],"intro":[{"sc":"egypt","n":"Just as Joseph had said, seven years of plenty came, then seven years of famine. Joseph had stored up grain, and people came from everywhere to buy food."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"One day, ten men came from Canaan and bowed down to Joseph. It was his brothers! They didn't recognise him."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Joseph tested them, and saw they had changed. Then he couldn't hold back his tears. \"I am Joseph, your brother!\""},{"sc":"egypt","w":"bjoseph","e":"big","t":"I am Joseph, your brother, whom you sent into Egypt! Don't be afraid. God sent me ahead of you to save lives."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"His brothers were terrified. But Joseph forgave them: \"You meant to do me evil, but God meant it for good, to save many people.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Forgiveness that saves","text":"Joseph had the power to punish his brothers. Instead he forgave them, and saved their lives. He saw God's bigger plan behind the pain. The greatest leaders use their power to forgive and to rescue, not to get revenge."},"order":["Seven years of plenty come","Seven years of famine follow","Joseph's brothers come to buy grain","They bow down to Joseph","Joseph says, \"I am Joseph your brother\"","Joseph forgives his brothers"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Joseph's brothers come to Egypt?","o":["To buy food during the famine","To find Joseph","To fight","On holiday"],"why":"There was famine everywhere."},{"q":"What did the brothers do when they met Joseph?","o":["Bowed down to him","Hugged him","Ran away","Laughed"],"why":"Just like his dreams!"},{"q":"What did Joseph say about what his brothers did?","o":["They meant evil, but God meant it for good","He would punish them","He would never forgive them","It didn't matter"],"why":"Genesis 50:20."}],"words":["FORGIVE","GRAIN","FAMINE","TEARS","FAMILY","SAVED"]},"gnV":{"passage":[[45,25,28],[46,1,7],[46,28,30],[47,7,12]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"The brothers raced home: \"Joseph is alive! He's ruler over all Egypt!\" Old Jacob's heart nearly stopped. He didn't believe them, until he saw the wagons Joseph had sent."},{"sc":"tents","w":"bjacob","e":"big","t":"Enough! My son Joseph is alive! I'll go and see him before I die."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"On the way, God spoke to Jacob at night: \"Don't be afraid to go down to Egypt. I'll make you a great nation there, and I'll bring you back again.\""},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Joseph drove his chariot out to meet his father. He threw his arms around him and wept for a long time."},{"sc":"egypt","n":"Jacob, 130 years old, met Pharaoh, and blessed him. Seventy people of Jacob's family settled in the best land of Egypt, called Goshen."}],"lesson":{"title":"God keeps families' stories going","text":"Jacob had grieved for Joseph for over twenty years. God brought them back together, and promised to be with the family even in a foreign land. Leaders trust that God can restore what seems lost for ever."},"order":["The brothers tell Jacob Joseph is alive","Jacob sees the wagons","God speaks to Jacob at night","Jacob's family travels to Egypt","Joseph and Jacob hug and weep","Jacob blesses Pharaoh"],"quiz":[{"q":"What made Jacob believe Joseph was alive?","o":["The wagons Joseph had sent","A letter","A dream","A song"],"why":"Genesis 45:27."},{"q":"How old was Jacob when he met Pharaoh?","o":["130","90","200","60"],"why":"Genesis 47:9."},{"q":"Where did Jacob's family settle?","o":["Goshen","Babel","Jericho","Bethel"],"why":"Genesis 47:6."}],"words":["JACOB","EGYPT","WAGONS","GOSHEN","PHARAOH","REUNITED"]},"gnW":{"passage":[[48,8,20],[49,1,12],[49,22,28]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","n":"Before he died, Jacob blessed Joseph's two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim. He crossed his arms on purpose, putting his right hand on the younger boy's head. \"The younger will be greater.\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"Then Jacob called all twelve sons to his bed. \"Gather round, and I'll tell you what will happen to you.\""},{"sc":"tents","n":"His words were honest. Reuben, unstable as water. Simeon and Levi, whose anger was cruel."},{"sc":"tents","n":"Judah, a lion's cub! \"The sceptre will not depart from Judah\": kings would come from him. And Joseph, a fruitful branch by a spring, whose branches climb over the wall."},{"sc":"tents","n":"These twelve sons became the twelve tribes of Israel. Then Jacob drew his feet up into the bed, breathed his last, and was gathered to his people."}],"lesson":{"title":"Words that shape the future","text":"Jacob's last words were honest about each son's character, and full of hope for their futures. Our choices shape our story. Leaders speak blessing and truth into the next generation."},"order":["Jacob blesses Manasseh and Ephraim","He crosses his arms on purpose","He gathers his twelve sons","He calls Judah a lion's cub","He calls Joseph a fruitful branch","Jacob dies"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which grandson got the greater blessing?","o":["The younger, Ephraim","The older, Manasseh","Neither","Benjamin"],"why":"Genesis 48:19."},{"q":"What animal did Jacob compare Judah to?","o":["A lion","An eagle","A wolf","A donkey"],"why":"Genesis 49:9."},{"q":"What did the twelve sons become?","o":["The twelve tribes of Israel","Twelve kings","Twelve cities","Twelve priests"],"why":"Genesis 49:28."}],"words":["BLESSING","JUDAH","LION","TRIBES","EPHRAIM","SCEPTRE"]}});
